A||||13||Toddster||A Fiero? Are you sure that is not a truck?||||1||
Z||000000||Toddster||07-22-2001||01:38 PM||||Folks, I'd like to hear your most eyebrow raising-Duh-what-are-you-talking-about Fiero story.<P>I'll start. I went to a Grand Auto the other day to get a set of upper engine gaskets for my Fiero. I told the lady at the parts counter (she was wearing a badge that said she was a "parts specialist") and said, "I need a set of upper engine Gaskets for a 1988 Pontiac Fiero with a 2.8 liter V-6 engine with A/C". She tappped on the keyboard for a moment and then looked at me and asked, "How do you spell 'Fiero'"? to which I replied, "F-i-e-r-o". She tapped on a few more keys and said, "I am not finding any Fiero trucks". "Trucks?", I said. "Isn't that a truck"? she said. "No, a Fiero is a two seater sports car" I explained. She tapped on the keys for a little while longer before excusing herself for a minute. She came back with a pimple faced kid who asked, "What kind of truck have you got?" I said, "A Ford Bronco". He said, "Oh,we have parts for that". I said, "Great, but my Bronco is running fine. I need parts for my Fiero...It's a Pontiac...two seater...sports car...vroom(making a hand gesture like a race car)". He said, "Pontiac doesn't make a two seater sports car". I said, "You are confused. They don't make trucks! They do, or did, make a two seater sports car, and I need a set of gaskets for it." He called the manager over whos said, "What can I do for you"? "I need a set of gaskets for my Fiero", I said frustratedly. He said, "I'm sorry but we don't carry Ferrari parts". I looked at him for 10 seconds and walked out.<P>I went to the Car Quest store up the road. The guy said, "Sure thing". Walked into the back room, brought out the package, and said, "$31.99". I gave him my credit card and was out the door in under 2 minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Toddster (edited 07-22-2001).]||||reg||1
